(i) An eligible bank may make an investment that exceeds fifteen per cent, but does not exceed twenty per cent, of the bank's capital and surplus without prior notification to, or approval by, the commissioner if the eligible bank submits an after-the-fact notice of the investment to the commissioner. The after-the-fact notice shall include:

(1) A description of the eligible bank's investments;

(2) The amount of the investment;

(3) The percentage of the eligible bank's capital and surplus represented by the investment that is the subject of the notice and the eligible bank's aggregate outstanding low-income housing commitments, including the investment that is the subject of the notice; and

(4) A statement certifying that the investment complies with the requirements of subsection (h).

